 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the county law and the New York city charter, in relation to\nthe docketing of adjudications of certain violations of laws enforced by the\nNew York city department of consumer affairs",
    "basePrintNo": "S8787",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8787-2019",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §918, County L; amd §2203, NYC Chart",
    "lawSection": "County Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S8787\n\nSPONSOR: THOMAS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the county law and the New York city charter, in\nrelation to the docketing of adjudications of certain violations of laws\nenforced by the New York city department of consumer affairs\n\n \nPURPOSE GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThe purpose of this bill relates to the court docketing of adjudications\nof certain violations of laws enforced by the New York City Department\nof Consumer Affairs (\"DCA\").\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSections. 1 and 2 would amend the County Law to authorize the Department\nof Consumer Affairs to readily docket in the civil court orders for\nrestitution and back wages and the like issued on behalf of consumers\nand workers, together with penalties associated with such orders for\nrestitution, unpaid wages and the like.\n\nSection 3 would amend the NYC Charter to establish appropriate proce-\ndural mechanisms for the conclusion and docketing of such orders in such\ncases.\n\nSection 4 is the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nBy authorizing DCA to readily enter and docket these judgments for\nrestitution, unpaid wages and the like in civil court, this legislation\nwould greatly assist consumers and workers in recovering restitution and\nlost wages ordered in proceedings brought by the NYC Department of\nConsumer Affairs. Included are businesses that have a particular oppor-\ntunity to harm consumers and workers, such as employment agencies,\ntobacco retail dealers, proprietors operating sidewalk stands, dealers\nof secondhand articles, home improvement contractors, debt collection\ncompanies and tow companies. By improving DCA's ability to promptly\ndocket these orders for restitution and unpaid wages, efforts to collect\nthese sums for consumers and workers will be expedited and enhanced.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew legislation.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone to the state.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately and shall only apply to decisions\nor orders issued on or after such effective date.\n",
